      {
        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 6 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"id\", \"bfi_1\", \"bfi_2\", \"bfi_2\", \"bfi_3\", \n\"bfi_4\"), Documented = c(\"no\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\", \"yes\"\n), Label = c(NA, \"Personality item 1\", \"Personality item 2\", \n\"Personality item 2\", \"Personality item 3\", \"Personality item 4\"\n), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(NA, \"bfi_1\", \"bfi_2\", \"bfi_2\", \"bfi_3\", \n\"bfi_4\"), Source = c(NA, \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\", \n\"codebook.csv\", \"codebook.csv\"), Status = c(\"unlabelled\", \"labelled\", \n\"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\", \"labelled\")), row.names = c(NA, \n6L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Scales",
          "We detected 1 column group (by shared abbreviation) that look like scales; 1 was matched to a named instrument from the paper text or dictionary. Groups we could not name are listed too — they are real scale-like column families whose instrument the manuscript did not identify. Identified scales are exported in the OpenScales OSD structure.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"s.csv\", Abbrev = \"BFI\", Columns = 5L, \n    \"Max item\" = \"4\", Scale = \"Big Five Inventory\", Confidence = \"medium\", \n    Source = \"manuscript\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 40, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "To let this tool (and anyone reusing the data) identify these scales with **high confidence**:\n- **Name the instrument in the manuscript with its abbreviation** — e.g. \"the Breakup Distress Scale (BDS)\" — matching the column prefix.\n- **Add a codebook** giving the item wording, or state the number of items (\"a 15-item scale\").",
          "LLM model 'mock/rv' reviewed ambiguous cases (parsed 0 files, matched 0 columns, merged 0 labels).",
          "#### Duplicated Column Names",
          "- **Duplicated column names in `s.csv`.** 1 column name appears more than once (worst: `bfi_2`×2), so 2 of the file's 6 columns share a name with another. This usually means a survey loop/merge exported repeated blocks without numbering each iteration; the repeats cannot be told apart and can only be documented once. Consider re-exporting with per-iteration column names."
        ]
      },
